    "abstract": "International audience",
    "field": "Antarctic precipitation modeling",
    "problem": "Climate models significantly overestimate current Antarctic precipitation, and the common practice of averaging all models for projections leads to a substantial underestimation of future snowfall's mitigating effect on sea-level rise.",
    "method": "To improve projections of future Antarctic precipitation, this paper evaluates CMIP5 models against CloudSat observations, isolating a more reliable subset of models to provide a constrained estimate of precipitation's future impact on sea level rise.",
    "task": "The task is to evaluate the performance of CMIP5 climate models in simulating current and projected Antarctic precipitation by comparing them to observational data, and to assess the implications for future sea-level rise.",
